    {
      "claim_id": "WF-EV-062: Option expiry and exercise fixing",
      "claim": "WF-EV-062: Option expiry and exercise fixing\n\nThe proposal checks published fixing indices against manually applied TP rates each day.\nThe fixing cut determines whether rates come from MDS or Trading Desk Voice Cuts.\nTolerance logic depends on fixing type; the page proposes a blotter for trades expiring Today and a comparison summary for Trade Control.\nTolerance values, source selection details, and the timezone for Today remain unknown.\n[Selected source, original lines 9\u201317](../../../../knowledge/evidence/sources/sha256/10dd09731fbd837022bebe18f107cbd8a7c33dc000239650860410423f825d45.md#L9-L17)\n",
      "support": [
        {
          "sha256": "10dd09731fbd837022bebe18f107cbd8a7c33dc000239650860410423f825d45",
          "range": [
            9,
            17
          ]
        }
      ],
      "confidence": "high for scoped source meaning; current applicability unknown"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "WF-EV-063: Trade-rule validation",
      "claim": "WF-EV-063: Trade-rule validation\n\nAfter receiving a trade from TDS3, RATAN builds trade facts and checks predefined rules.\nIt records violations in the Ratan Exception Platform for Trade Review.\nWhen no rule matches, the workflow closes any prior-version exception.\nWhen a rule matches, it closes the prior-version exception and creates one for the current version.\nThe result appears in the exception blotter.\nThe review table is blank; its instruction says to set status to Published after review.\n[Selected source, original lines 3\u201317](../../../../knowledge/evidence/sources/sha256/2f4fe2c7f6677d661043b2a9b5b5e3f034a894e40d53435ebdd2f93436dbad55.md#L3-L17)\n",
